Ned Stark's last surviving son?

272
00:29:20,810 --> 00:29:23,150
Jon Snow is a bastard, not a Stark.

273
00:29:24,120 --> 00:29:26,220
So was I, Father.

274
00:29:26,220 --> 00:29:28,160
Your hold on the North will never be secure

275
00:29:28,170 --> 00:29:31,010
as long as a Stark can walk through that door.

276
00:29:31,140 --> 00:29:33,710
Castle Black isn't defended on the southern side.

277
00:29:33,810 --> 00:29:35,850
And the few men left are barely men at all.

278
00:29:35,850 --> 00:29:37,390
Farm boys and thieves.

279
00:29:37,390 --> 00:29:41,590
With a small force, we could storm the castle, kill Jon Snow--

280
00:29:41,590 --> 00:29:44,120
Murder the Lord Commander of the Night's Watch?

281
00:29:44,460 --> 00:29:47,180
You'd unite every house in the North against us.

282
00:29:48,710 --> 00:29:51,170
We don't need every house in the North.

283
00:29:51,170 --> 00:29:53,310
The Umbers, the Manderlys, and the Karstarks

284
00:29:53,310 --> 00:29:56,040
command more soldiers than all the other houses combined.

285
00:29:57,610 --> 00:30:00,720
With their support, none could challenge us.

286
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:02,080
The Starks lost my house

287
00:30:02,080 --> 00:30:04,590
the day King Robb cut off my father's head.

288
00:30:05,310 --> 00:30:07,670
It's time for new blood in the North.

289
00:30:16,870 --> 00:30:19,520
If you acquire a reputation as a mad dog,

290
00:30:19,520 --> 00:30:21,360
you'll be treated as a mad dog.

291
00:30:21,830 --> 00:30:24,490
Taken out back and slaughtered for pig feed.

292
00:30:25,430 --> 00:30:26,880
My lords.

293
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:30,050
Lady Walda has given birth.

294
00:30:30,500 --> 00:30:31,880
A boy.

295
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:34,860
Red-cheeked and healthy.

296
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:37,150
My congratulations, Lord Bolton.

297
00:30:47,430 --> 00:30:49,260
Congratulations, Father.

298
00:30:50,950 --> 00:30:53,310
I look forward to meeting my new brother.

299
00:30:58,030 --> 00:31:00,360
You'll always be my firstborn.

300
00:31:01,580 --> 00:31:03,380
Thank you for saying that.

301
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:06,340
It means a great deal to me.

302
00:31:43,220 --> 00:31:44,670
Maester Wolkan,

303
00:31:45,940 --> 00:31:49,110
send ravens to all the northern houses. Roose Bolton is dead.

304
00:31:50,650 --> 00:31:52,610
Poisoned by our enemies.

305
00:31:59,830 --> 00:32:01,360
How did he die?

306
00:32:05,100 --> 00:32:07,760
Poisoned by his enemies.

307
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:10,660
You're talking to your lord. Use respect.

308
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:13,880
Forgive me, my lord.

309
00:32:17,510 --> 00:32:19,510
Send for Lady Walda and the baby.

310
00:32:20,810 --> 00:32:22,780
She's resting, my lord.

311
00:32:26,500 --> 00:32:28,100
At once, my lord.

312
00:32:53,550 --> 00:32:55,150
There he is.

313
00:32:55,370 --> 00:32:57,040
Isn't he wonderful?

314
00:33:01,140 --> 00:33:02,670
May I hold him?

315
00:33:03,920 --> 00:33:05,730
Of-- of course.

316
00:33:15,950 --> 00:33:17,510
Little brother.

317
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:21,290
Lord Bolton sent for us.

318
00:33:21,290 --> 00:33:22,860
Have you seen him?

319
00:33:31,370 --> 00:33:34,460
Of course. Follow me, Mother.

320
00:33:52,250 --> 00:33:53,910
Where is Lord Bolton?

321
00:34:04,010 --> 00:34:05,150
Down!

322
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:09,040
It's all right. Come on, shh.

323
00:34:09,670 --> 00:34:12,470
It's cold out here, Ramsay. I need to feed him.

324
00:34:18,640 --> 00:34:21,810
Ramsay, where is your father?

325
00:34:22,870 --> 00:34:24,240
Ramsay.

326
00:34:32,820 --> 00:34:34,440
Where is Lord Bolton?

327
00:34:41,520 --> 00:34:43,180
I am Lord Bolton.

328
00:34:53,600 --> 00:34:54,730
Ramsay.

329
00:34:55,630 --> 00:34:56,980
Ramsay, please.

330
00:34:57,270 --> 00:34:59,950
I'll leave Winterfell. I'll go back to the Riverlands.

331
00:35:05,540 --> 00:35:06,870
Please.

332
00:35:08,010 --> 00:35:09,090
Ramsay.

333
00:35:11,380 --> 00:35:13,000
He's your brother.

334
00:35:16,060 --> 00:35:18,360
I prefer being an only child.

335
00:35:38,890 --> 00:35:41,900
I saw her with a man.

336
00:35:41,900 --> 00:35:43,610
I don't think he hurt her.

337
00:35:43,730 --> 00:35:46,490
She didn't want to leave him, he didn't want to leave her.

338
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:50,940
You don't know which way she went?

339
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:52,930
I spent three days looking for her.

340
00:35:53,370 --> 00:35:55,010
She disappeared.

341
00:35:57,520 --> 00:35:58,810
How'd she look?

342
00:35:58,810 --> 00:36:00,160
She looked good.

343
00:36:01,180 --> 00:36:03,990
She wasn't exactly dressed like a lady.

344
00:36:05,180 --> 00:36:06,780
No, she wouldn't be.

345
00:36:09,180 --> 00:36:10,960
What happened at Winterfell?

346
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:25,400
I should have gone with you while I had the chance.

347
00:36:26,900 --> 00:36:29,360
It was a difficult choice, my lady.

348
00:36:33,860 --> 00:36:36,270
We've all had to make difficult choices.

349
00:36:57,110 --> 00:36:59,090
We shouldn't be lighting fires.

350
00:36:59,100 --> 00:37:00,400
It's not safe.

351
00:37:00,400 --> 00:37:01,750
He won't stop hunting us.

352
00:37:01,750 --> 00:37:03,560
We just have to make it to Castle Black.

353
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:06,190
Once we're with Jon, Ramsay won't be able to touch us.

354
00:37:06,190 --> 00:37:08,680
Jon will have me killed the moment I step through the gate.

355
00:37:08,680 --> 00:37:10,220
I won't let him.

356
00:37:10,580 --> 00:37:12,770
I'll tell him the truth about Bran and Rickon.

357
00:37:14,790 --> 00:37:17,990
And the truth about the farm boys I killed in their place.

358
00:37:18,020 --> 00:37:20,740
And the truth about Ser Rodrik, who I beheaded.

359
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:26,300
And the truth about Robb, who I betrayed.

360
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:31,060
When you take the black, all your crimes are forgiven.

361
00:37:31,060 --> 00:37:32,820
I don't want to be forgiven.

362
00:37:35,370 --> 00:37:38,780
I can never make amends to your family for the things I've done.

363
00:37:40,910 --> 00:37:43,290
They'll keep you safer than I ever could.

364
00:37:48,390 --> 00:37:50,160
You're not coming with us?

365
00:37:53,190 --> 00:37:55,520
I would have taken you all the way to the Wall.

366
00:37:57,430 --> 00:37:59,330
I would have died to get you there.

367
00:38:16,330 --> 00:38:18,190
May I take one of the horses?

368
00:38:22,250 --> 00:38:23,810
Where will you go?

369
00:38:27,300 --> 00:38:28,470
Home.

370
00:38:37,790 --> 00:38:40,340
The Glovers have retaken Deepwood Motte.

371
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:43,940
And the ironborn who held it?

372
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:47,130
They died fighting to a man.

373
00:38:48,910 --> 00:38:51,070
What is dead may never die.

374
00:38:51,270 --> 00:38:53,070
What is dead may never die.

375
00:38:53,410 --> 00:38:54,930
But they did

376
00:38:55,300 --> 00:38:57,780
and our invasion died with them.

377
00:38:58,570 --> 00:39:01,530
Deepwood Motte was our last stronghold on the mainland.

378
00:39:01,530 --> 00:39:03,190
Then we will take more.

379
00:39:03,190 --> 00:39:06,650
Why? For more pinecones and rocks?

380
00:39:08,900 --> 00:39:11,230
Because I order it.

381
00:39:11,230 --> 00:39:13,280
We can defeat anyone at sea,

382
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:15,490
but we'll never hold lands and castles

383
00:39:15,490 --> 00:39:16,900
against mainland armies.

384
00:39:16,910 --> 00:39:19,760
Not if our captains defy my orders,

385
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:24,140
abandon their posts, and sacrifice our men on foolish missions.

386
00:39:24,140 --> 00:39:26,220
I won't apologize for trying to rescue Theon.

387
00:39:26,220 --> 00:39:27,370
Then where is he?

388
00:39:27,370 --> 00:39:28,930
Where is your kingdom?

389
00:39:30,410 --> 00:39:33,900
We took those castles because the northerners marched off to war.

390
00:39:33,950 --> 00:39:35,850
That war is over.

391
00:39:35,850 --> 00:39:38,070
The last time we provoked them too far,

392
00:39:38,070 --> 00:39:40,520
I watched from that window as they breached our walls

393
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:42,340
and knocked down our towers.

394
00:39:42,620 --> 00:39:44,600
I lost two brothers that day.

395
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:46,960
And I lost three sons.

396
00:39:48,850 --> 00:39:50,810
The War of the Five Kings, they call it.

397
00:39:50,810 --> 00:39:52,690
Well, the other four are dead.

398
00:39:52,690 --> 00:39:54,410
When you rule the Iron Islands,

399
00:39:54,410 --> 00:39:56,000
you can wage all the peace you want.

400
00:39:56,010 --> 00:39:57,910
But for now, shut your mouth and obey

401
00:39:57,910 --> 00:40:00,980
or I will make another heir who will.

402
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:40,880
Let me pass.

403
00:40:43,950 --> 00:40:46,860
You fool, move aside for your king.

404
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:49,940
Haven't I always, brother?

405
00:40:59,950 --> 00:41:04,300
I thought you'd be rotting under some foreign sea by now.

406
00:41:05,290 --> 00:41:07,510
What is dead may never die.

407
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:13,070
Has the custom changed since I've been gone?

408
00:41:13,200 --> 00:41:15,470
Aren't you supposed to repeat the words?

409
00:41:15,710 --> 00:41:18,530
You can mock our god without my help.

410
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,620
I don't mock the Drowned God.

411
00:41:21,680 --> 00:41:23,880
I am the Drowned God.

412
00:41:24,540 --> 00:41:26,180
From Oldtown to Qarth,

413
00:41:26,180 --> 00:41:29,800
when men see my sails, they pray.

414
00:41:40,270 --> 00:41:41,790
You're old, brother.

415
00:41:42,370 --> 00:41:44,170
You've had your time.

416
00:41:44,310 --> 00:41:46,060
Now let another rule.

417
00:41:47,380 --> 00:41:49,760
I heard you lost your mind

418
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:53,050
during a storm on the Jade Sea.

419
00:41:53,270 --> 00:41:58,000
They tied you to the mast to keep you from jumping overboard.

420
00:41:58,930 --> 00:41:59,840
They did.

421
00:42:00,220 --> 00:42:04,000
And when the storm passed, you cut out their tongues.

422
00:42:04,980 --> 00:42:06,470
I needed silence.

423
00:42:07,990 --> 00:42:10,180
What kind of an ironborn

424
00:42:10,330 --> 00:42:13,610
loses his senses during a storm?

425
00:42:15,340 --> 00:42:17,460
I am the storm, brother.

426
00:42:18,770 --> 00:42:20,520
The first storm and the last.

427
00:42:22,300 --> 00:42:23,790
And you're in my way.

428
00:43:02,460 --> 00:43:05,700
Lord, take your servant Balon back beneath the waves.

429
00:43:06,840 --> 00:43:09,790
Feed the creatures of your kingdom on his flesh.

430
00:43:10,350 --> 00:43:12,280
Pull his bones down to your depths

431
00:43:12,280 --> 00:43:15,110
to rest beside his ancestors and his children.

432
00:43:15,110 --> 00:43:17,350
What is dead may never die.

433
00:43:27,120 --> 00:43:28,920
I'm going to find out who did this.

434
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:32,330
I'm going to feed them to the sharks while they live.

435
00:43:34,450 --> 00:43:36,400
I swear it by the Salt Throne.

436
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:39,740
The Salt Throne is not yours to swear upon,

437
00:43:40,060 --> 00:43:42,160
not unless the kingsmoot chooses you.

438
00:43:42,160 --> 00:43:44,070
My father would have wanted me to rule.

439
00:43:44,070 --> 00:43:47,200
Your father does not get to choose. The law is clear.

440
00:43:50,050 --> 00:43:51,150
Perhaps you'll win.

441
00:43:52,080 --> 00:43:55,030
Perhaps you'll be the first woman in history to rule the ironborn.

442
00:43:56,560 --> 00:43:57,670
And perhaps not.

443
00:44:15,430 --> 00:44:16,260
Come in.

444
00:44:23,050 --> 00:44:25,810
I'm sorry, my lady. Didn't mean to interrupt.

445
00:44:26,700 --> 00:44:28,280
You interrupt nothing.

446
00:44:40,570 --> 00:44:43,080
I assume you know why I'm here.

447
00:44:44,830 --> 00:44:46,520
I will after you tell me.

448
00:44:47,240 --> 00:44:48,800
It's about the Lord Commander.

449
00:44:48,870 --> 00:44:50,890
The former Lord Commander.

450
00:44:52,570 --> 00:44:53,740
Does he have to be?

451
00:44:57,730 --> 00:44:59,130
What are you asking?

452
00:45:03,530 --> 00:45:07,440
Do you know of any magic...

453
00:45:08,890 --> 00:45:10,020
that could help him?

454
00:45:11,470 --> 00:45:12,540
Bring him back?

455
00:45:12,700 --> 00:45:14,940
If you want to help him, leave him be.

456
00:45:14,940 --> 00:45:15,870
Can it be done?

457
00:45:17,930 --> 00:45:19,780
There are some with this power.

458
00:45:19,780 --> 00:45:22,550
- How? - I don't know.

459
00:45:22,550 --> 00:45:23,930
Have you seen it done?

460
00:45:27,420 --> 00:45:29,500
I met a man who came back from the dead,

461
00:45:29,500 --> 00:45:31,090
but the priest who did it--

462
00:45:33,350 --> 00:45:34,580
it shouldn't have been possible.

463
00:45:34,580 --> 00:45:37,970
But it was. It could be now.

464
00:45:38,960 --> 00:45:40,040
Not for me.

465
00:45:44,620 --> 00:45:45,570
Not for you?

466
00:45:50,730 --> 00:45:53,520
I saw you drink poison that should have killed you.

467
00:45:54,510 --> 00:45:57,010
I saw you give birth to a demon made of shadows.

468
00:45:57,010 --> 00:45:58,650
Everything I believed,

469
00:46:00,040 --> 00:46:02,650
the great victory I saw in the flames,

470
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:04,820
all of it was a lie.

471
00:46:09,540 --> 00:46:11,230
You were right all along.

472
00:46:11,980 --> 00:46:13,760
The Lord never spoke to me.

473
00:46:14,680 --> 00:46:15,650
Fuck him, then.

474
00:46:16,040 --> 00:46:17,190
Fuck all of them.

475
00:46:20,020 --> 00:46:22,760
I'm not a devout man, obviously.

476
00:46:23,620 --> 00:46:27,020
Seven gods, drowned gods, tree gods, it's all the same.

477
00:46:30,340 --> 00:46:32,580
I'm not asking the Lord of Light for help.

478
00:46:33,610 --> 00:46:37,500
I'm asking the woman who showed me that miracles exist.

479
00:46:39,690 --> 00:46:41,540
I never had this gift.

480
00:46:41,910 --> 00:46:43,270
Have you ever tried?

481
00:50:27,810 --> 00:50:28,800
Please.

